[statement]
A provider at no version answers an entry admitting earlier versions only
as it answers the name alone: with a priority. `a` provides `v` at no
version and states none, and apk refuses `v<3`, as it refuses `v`
(`a-provider-at-no-version-answers-an-entry-admitting-earlier-versions`).

[repository]
P:a
V:1
p:v

[request]
v<3

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   v (virtual):
|     note: please select one of the 'provided by'
|           packages explicitly
|     provided by: a
|     required by: world[v<3]
refused
